Chapter: SudokuWasm
  cites Games chapter Sudoku
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Sudoku, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. Eighty-one cells are past an i32, so the page
 holds the state's address.

 `sudoku-solve` and `sudoku-remove-cells` both write the grid with
 `list-set-at`, which mutates in place. The solver depends on that -- it
 clears a cell to backtrack -- but it means a puzzle and its solution are
 otherwise the same list, so `sd-wasm-solve` and `sd-wasm-remove` copy
 first and a page or a grader can hold both.

 We say:

Section: Copying

  sd-copy-grid : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  sd-copy-grid (src) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 81 then acc
    else sd-copy-grid src (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  sd-copy-state : SudokuState -> SudokuState
  sd-copy-state (st) =
    SudokuState { grid = sd-copy-grid (st.grid) 0 [], iterations = st.iterations }

Section: The Browser Interface

  sd-wasm-new : Integer -> SudokuState
  sd-wasm-new (seed) = sudoku-new (rng-new seed)

  sd-wasm-cell : SudokuState, Integer -> Integer
  sd-wasm-cell (st) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= 81 then (-1)
    else list-at (st.grid) i

  sd-wasm-iterations : SudokuState -> Integer
  sd-wasm-iterations (st) = st.iterations

  sd-wasm-givens : SudokuState -> Integer
  sd-wasm-givens (st) = sudoku-count-givens (st.grid)

  sd-wasm-first-empty : SudokuState -> Integer
  sd-wasm-first-empty (st) = sudoku-find-empty (st.grid) 0

  sd-wasm-valid : SudokuState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sd-wasm-valid (st) (row) (col) (val) =
    if row < 0 then (-1)
    else if row >= 9 then (-1)
    else if col < 0 then (-1)
    else if col >= 9 then (-1)
    else if val < 1 then (-1)
    else if val > 9 then (-1)
    else if sudoku-is-valid (st.grid) row col val then 1
    else 0

  sd-wasm-solve : SudokuState -> SudokuState
  sd-wasm-solve (st) = sudoku-solve (sd-copy-state st)

  sd-wasm-remove : SudokuState, Integer, Integer -> SudokuState
  sd-wasm-remove (st) (seed) (count) =
    if count < 0 then st
    else sudoku-remove-cells (sd-copy-state st) (rng-new seed) count

Section: Playing By Hand

 `sd-wasm-solve` fills the whole grid in one call, which is a solver and not
 a game. These write ONE cell, so a person can.

 `sudoku-is-valid` asks whether a value may go at a row and column by
 scanning the row, the column and the box -- and it does NOT exclude the
 target cell from that scan. So overwriting a cell that already holds a
 digit has to CLEAR it first, or the cell's own value is found in its own
 row and the placement is refused as a duplicate of itself. Writing into an
 empty cell has no such problem, which is exactly why this would have
 survived a test that only ever filled blanks.

  sd-set-cell : SudokuState, Integer, Integer -> SudokuState
  sd-set-cell (st) (i) (val) =
    SudokuState { grid = list-set-at (st.grid) i val, iterations = st.iterations }

  sd-wasm-place : SudokuState, Integer, Integer -> SudokuState
  sd-wasm-place (st) (i) (val) =
    if i < 0 then st
    else if i >= 81 then st
    else if val < 0 then st
    else if val > 9 then st
    else if val == 0 then sd-set-cell (sd-copy-state st) i 0
    else let cleared = sd-set-cell (sd-copy-state st) i 0
    in if sudoku-is-valid (cleared.grid) (i / 9) (rng-mod i 9) val then sd-set-cell cleared i val
    else st

 Whether a digit may go in a cell, asked by INDEX rather than by row and
 column, because that is what a page holds after a click. Same clearing rule
 as above.

  sd-wasm-fits : SudokuState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sd-wasm-fits (st) (i) (val) =
    if i < 0 then 0
    else if i >= 81 then 0
    else if val < 1 then 0
    else if val > 9 then 0
    else let cleared = sd-set-cell (sd-copy-state st) i 0
    in if sudoku-is-valid (cleared.grid) (i / 9) (rng-mod i 9) val then 1 else 0

 How many cells are still empty, so the page can say how far along you are
 without walking the grid itself.

  sd-wasm-empty-count : SudokuState -> Integer
  sd-wasm-empty-count (st) = sd-count-empty (st.grid) 0 0

  sd-count-empty : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sd-count-empty (grid) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 81 then acc
    else if list-at grid i == 0 then sd-count-empty grid (i + 1) (acc + 1)
    else sd-count-empty grid (i + 1) acc

Section: The Pinned Run

  sd-wasm-run : SudokuResult
  sd-wasm-run = run-sudoku-solve

  sd-wasm-res-solved : SudokuResult -> Integer
  sd-wasm-res-solved (r) = if r.solved then 1 else 0

  sd-wasm-res-iterations : SudokuResult -> Integer
  sd-wasm-res-iterations (r) = r.iterations

  sd-wasm-res-givens : SudokuResult -> Integer
  sd-wasm-res-givens (r) = r.givens

